<title>USA: Thomas &amp; Betts sales hurt by currency.</title>
<headline>Thomas &amp; Betts sales hurt by currency.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomas &amp; Betts Corp said on Tuesday that negative currency translation lowered the increase in its first-quarter net sales by a full percentage point, or $4.8 million.</p>
<p>Thomas &amp; Betts said its net sales were $504.3 million, up four percent from $486.7 million for the first quarter of 1996. Thomas &amp; Betts reported net income of $0.55 per share for the first quarter, up from $0.49 from the same period the year before.</p>
<p>Thomas &amp; Betts makes connectors and components for the electrical and electronics markets.</p>
</text>
